<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n114863" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρῡσό-δετος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
		also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Alc.
			33
		</span></i>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέω</span>(A)):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bound with gold, set in gold,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφρηγίς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.41
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>overlaid</i> or <i>enriched with gold,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλεφαντίναν λάβαν τῷ ξίφεος
					χρυσοδέταν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alc.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. κέρας,</span> of a lyre,
				<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				244
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. ἕρκεσι
			γυναικῶν,</span> of the <i>golden</i> necklace with which
			Eriphyle was bribed, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>El.</u>
				838
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περόναι χ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					805
				</span></i>
			(lyr.): metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. σώματος ἀλκήν</span>”
				<i>in golden armour,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					382
				</span></i>
			 (anap.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
